    {
        "id": "c0ffee00rrcomment01",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "c0ffee00roborocktab",
        "name": "How to use this example",
        "info": "1. Open the roborock device config and add a roborock account. Sign in (email code, password, or a Home Assistant session) and click Done. Do not deploy yet.\n2. Fetch devices from account and pick the vacuum. Find on LAN fills the IP when UDP 58866 can hear the robot.\n3. Done, then Deploy once. Inject start / dock / status. Output 1 is the command result. Output 2 is status.\n\nShow maps & rooms on the device is a read-only list of map ids and room ids. It does not switch floors. Switch with {\"command\":\"map\",\"mapFlag\":1} and clean with {\"command\":\"rooms\",\"segments\":[16]}. {\"command\":\"map_rooms\"} returns the same list.\nlocal_key is stored in credentials and is intentionally absent from this example.\nThe local key changes after a Wi-Fi reset — fetch it again if commands start timing out.\n\nThis package is unofficial and is not affiliated with Roborock.",
        "x": 260,
        "y": 80,
        "wires": []
    },
